restart was acknowledged, polling observed connection loss then recovery, a new boot identity was confirmed, and DNS/service state was re-verified post-restart: node1 (cmd-cf138ea2126c4900, cmd-d57e9b27796b41ad, cmd-dc47e05d7ba5499a, cmd-19ce724438664dcd, cmd-e07ca3fb0ecf4619), node2 (cmd-600c62cba3a244d1, cmd-9462ca46153641b6, cmd-4561e4553ef1491c, cmd-b01b6d9cc4c142a6, cmd-7a2e89f269ef46b5), node3 (cmd-8193576b03a94bd2, cmd-cef262e9a40749d4, cmd-b465be7324f14ef5, cmd-ae3144bb985342ab), node4 (cmd-2ace8a1f8dd14594, cmd-50a3935130344c46, cmd-6bc93fd95fe1485e, cmd-6b1d018bce244e5f). Fixed lifecycle snapshots corroborate boot-identity changes on all four nodes.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-cf138ea2126c4900\",\"cmd-d57e9b27796b41ad\",\"cmd-dc47e05d7ba5499a\",\"cmd-19ce724438664dcd\",\"cmd-e07ca3fb0ecf4619\",\"cmd-600c62cba3a244d1\",\"cmd-9462ca46153641b6\",\"cmd-4561e4553ef1491c\",\"cmd-b01b6d9cc4c142a6\",\"cmd-7a2e89f269ef46b5\",\"cmd-8193576b03a94bd2\",\"cmd-cef262e9a40749d4\",\"cmd-b465be7324f14ef5\",\"cmd-ae3144bb985342ab\",\"cmd-2ace8a1f8dd14594\",\"cmd-50a3935130344c46\",\"cmd-6bc93fd95fe1485e\",\"cmd-6b1d018bce244e5f\",\"global:after_executor:node1:boot-identity\",\"global:after_executor:node2:boot-identity\",\"global:after_executor:node3:boot-identity\",\"global:after_executor:node4:boot-identity\"]}],\"confidence\":0.9,\"operational_hygiene\":{\"score\":0.72,\"summary\":\"Most executor mutations were directly tied to the task (VyOS static-host-mapping/dns-forwarding config, OPNsense host-override) or to the mandated restart-evidence protocol, and were fully verified. However, on node2 the executor made an initial malformed Unbound host-override XML edit (cmd-2cb9fa08d25b487d) using an incorrect schema (host/domain/ip instead of hostname/domain/rr/server), which broke unbound-checkconf (cmd-8be984ad59524a74, cmd-04991543366f4ea0) before being corrected (cmd-bd08b3fec8624190); this counts as an unnecessary/incorrect mutation even though it was subsequently fixed an