mal DHCP-provided DNS settings, though this is a reasonable proxy for the same behavior.\"]}","structured_output":{"requirements":[{"id":"node1-resolves-app-to-node3","requirement":"node1 (VyOS, lan-a router) resolves app.internal to node3's address (10.100.13.12) for lan-a hosts","status":"satisfied","summary":"node1 was configured with a static-host-mapping for app.internal -> 10.100.13.12 plus DNS forwarding, committed and saved (cmd-18c2e895d27a4503). Local dig on node1 and nslookup from node3 both returned 10.100.13.12 before restart (cmd-a22b462711f3414c, cmd-223d4db0dbdc44eb), and the same resolution was re-verified from node3 after node1's restart (cmd-e07ca3fb0ecf4619, cmd-2f043a2d29164296), confirming persistence across a reboot.","evidence_ids":["cmd-18c2e895d27a4503","cmd-a22b462711f3414c","cmd-223d4db0dbdc44eb","cmd-e07ca3fb0ecf4619","cmd-2f043a2d29164296"]},{"id":"node2-resolves-app-to-node4","requirement":"node2 (OPNsense, lan-b router) resolves app.internal to node4's address (10.100.13.13) for lan-b hosts","status":"satisfied","summary":"After correcting an initial malformed Unbound host-override schema (host/domain/ip instead of hostname/domain/rr/server, which broke unbound-checkconf), the executor applied a schema-correct host override, restarted unbound, and confirmed host_entries.conf and live drill/nslookup queries returned 10.100.13.13 both from node2 itself and from node4 (cmd-e5fc7d91506d49a7, cmd-07e60535acb94bf9, cmd-aa0237bdef7b4bc1). Resolution was re-confirmed from node4 after node2's restart (cmd-7a2e89f269ef46b5, cmd-a90b2be18671484b).","evidence_ids":["cmd-2cb9fa08d25b487d","cmd-bd08b3fec8624190","cmd-e5fc7d91506d49a7","cmd-07e60535acb94bf9","cmd-aa0237bdef7b4bc1","cmd-7a2e89f269ef46b5","cmd-a90b2be18671484b"]},{"id":"split-dns-persists-across-restart","requirement":"Split DNS behavior (each host resolves app.internal only to its own side's service address) persists after routers restart, consistent with the provider-wide restart-evidence protocol applied to all four nodes","status":"satisfied","summary":"For all four nodes, pre-restart boot identity and working DNS answers were captured, a restart was acknowledged, polling observed connection loss then recovery, a new boot identity was confirmed, and DNS/service state was re-verified post-restart: node1 (cmd-cf138ea2126c4900, cmd-d57e9b27796b41ad, cmd-dc47e05d7ba5499a, cmd-19ce724438664dcd, cmd-e07ca3fb0ecf4619), node2 (cmd-600c62cba3a244d1, cmd-9462ca46153641b6, cmd-4561e4553ef1491c, cmd-b01b6d9cc4c142a6, cmd-7a2e89f269ef46b5), node3 (cmd-8193576b03a94bd2, cmd-cef262e9a40749d4, cmd-b465be7324f14ef5, cmd-ae3144bb985342ab), node4 (cmd-2ace8a1f8dd14594, cmd-50a3935130344c46, cmd-6bc93fd95fe1485e, cmd-6b1d018bce244e5f). Fixed lifecycle snapshots corroborate boot-identity changes on all four nodes.","evidence_ids":["cmd-cf138ea2126c4900","cmd-d57e9b27796b41ad","cmd-dc47e05d7ba5499a","cmd-19ce724438664dcd","cmd-e07ca3fb0ecf4619","cmd-600c62cba3a244d1","cmd-9462ca46153641b6","cmd-4561e4553ef1491c","cmd-b01b6d9cc4c142a6","cmd-7a2e89f269ef46b5","cmd-8193576b03a94bd2","cmd-cef262e9a40749d4","cmd-b465be7324f14ef5","cmd-ae3144bb985342ab","cmd-2ace8a1f8dd14594","cmd-50a3935130344c46","cmd-6bc93fd95fe1485e","cmd-6b1d018bce244e5f","global:after_executor:node1:boot-identity","global:after_executor:node2:boot-identity","global:after_executor:node3:boot-identity","global:after_executor:node4:boot-identity"]}],"confidence":0.9,"operational_hygiene":{"score":0.72,"summary":"Most executor mutations were directly tied to the task (VyOS static-host-mapping/dns-forwarding config, OPNsense host-override) or to the mandated restart-evidence protocol, and were fully verified. However, on node2 the executor made an initial malformed Unbound host-override XML edit (cmd-2cb9fa08d25b487d) using an incorrect schema (host/domain/ip instead of hostname/domain/rr/server), which broke unbound-checkconf (cmd-8be984ad59524a74, cmd-04991543366f4ea0) before being corrected (cmd-bd